        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Reserve and audit requirements create compliance costs that structurally favor large, well-capitalized issuers (Tether, Circle) over smaller or decentralized alternatives like DAI or algorithmic stablecoins.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Traditional finance entrants (Morgan Stanley stablecoin reserves portfolio, banks pursuing issuance under FDIC rulemaking) could compress margins and market share for crypto-native issuers.",
